Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 19:21:29 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] iOS: laptop mode on foldables, screen fit, and game data from
 your own server

The per-game iPhone app splits the screen at the hinge of a half-folded foldable (UIHinge, iOS 27.1: the game
upright, the pad flat) and fits the picture by DM_SCREEN_FIT (fit, zoom, stretch). Its game data (romfs.img and the
shader libraries, read in place from msl.tar) downloads in the background from a server of the player's own,
published by scripts/publish_gamedata.py (data/<title>/<build>/, the IPA and an AltStore source.json). A slim IPA
packs add-on content up to DM_AOC_MAX_MB (64 MB by default).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Upstream-Status: fork-only
Reason: the Duo's laptop mode and a self-hosted game data server for the per-game iPhone app
Issue: none (the fork Valtterios/NX2Apple has no issue tracker; branch duo-laptop-mode)

