+### Screen fit
+
+How the 16:9 picture meets a screen of another shape (iPhone only). **Fit** keeps the whole picture with black bars, **Fill (crop edges)** zooms until the bars are gone and cuts off what overflows, **Fill (stretch)** stretches the picture to the screen.
+
 ## Controls
 
 ### Touch feedback
 
 A light tap from the phone when you press an on-screen button.
 
+### Laptop mode (automatic)
+
+On a foldable iPhone (iOS 27.1 or later), half-folding it like a laptop puts the game on the upright half and the on-screen controls on the flat half; unfolded or closed, the usual landscape layout returns. It has no switch: `DM_HINGE_SPLIT=0` in `env.txt` turns it off, and `DM_HINGE_SPLIT_AT` moves the fold line (a fraction of the height, `0.2` to `0.8`; the middle by default).
+
 ### Game rumble
 
 The game's vibration, on the phone or on a connected controller.
